description:
BUG (confirmed silent miscompile, clang -O1 reachable). A reconverging quantum-controlled arm (diamond / symmetric / nested-AND / gated-switch) that contains a CLASSICAL side effect (an untainted-operand call/store/etc. that is not a cq_phi gate, the terminator, or a measure/ret) is silently accepted, and the side effect is hoisted to run UNCONDITIONALLY on every path.

ROOT CAUSE. armEscapesOrCollect (ControlDetection.cpp:299-320) only diagnoses ReturnInst / isMeasureCall / out-of-region br, and only COLLECTS cq_phi calls into Shadow; every OTHER instruction is silently skipped (the for-loop has no else/default reject). substituteArm rewrites only Shadow (cq_phi) to controlled form; CFGLinearization then splices the ENTIRE arm body (all but the terminator) unconditionally into the predecessor (CFGLinearization.cpp:51; ControlledLowering.cpp:203/205/240; linearizeNested:160). Net: a side effect the source guarded on a quantum predicate now fires on every path. verify-clean, no diagnostic. The team already plugged this class on the switch-normalization paths (empty-arm requirement SwitchNormalization.cpp:51-58; unexpected-instruction decline :255) and via the tainted-memory pre-scan (ControlDetection.cpp:204), but the GENERAL arm walk has no 'gate-bodies-only' guard.

REPRO (clang -O1, llvm@19 19.1.7, libCQPass.so @ b062f2d; /tmp/cqcheck/classical_se2.c):

  extern void sink(int);
  int f(int x, int cnd) {
      int q = cq_theta(x, 0.5);
      int p = cq_theta(cnd, 0.3);
      int r = q;
      if (p > 0) { r = cq_phi(q, 0.1); sink(42); }   // gate body + classical side effect
      return cq_measure(r);
  }

Lowered output: the controlled rotation cqrt_rz_i32_controlled([p>0], %h, 0.1) is emitted, but `tail call void @sink(i32 42)` is spliced into the linearized block UNCONDITIONALLY (no flag control, no br/label remain). sink() now runs even when p<=0. opt -passes=verify CLEAN, exit 0, NO diagnostic.

(NB: a no-merge-phi variant — `if(p>0){ cq_phi(q); sink(); } return cq_measure(q);` — is instead LOUDLY declined by the catch-all 'control flow under quantum control', because matchDiamond needs a gate-handle merge phi. The silent splice only bites when matchDiamond/Symmetric/NestedAnd/gated actually MATCHES, i.e. there is a proper merge phi AND a stray side effect.)

RELATED (same class, same fix family): the nested-AND shape `if(a){ <stmt>; if(b) gate; }` escape-guards ONLY the inner gate Arm (ControlDetection.cpp:532), never the intermediate Mid block; linearizeNested (ControlledLowering.cpp:160) splices Mid's body unconditionally — a side-effecting Mid stmt runs unconditionally with no diagnostic.

RECOMMENDED FIX (per-gap optimal, user-chosen 2026-06-03 = LOUD DECLINE, PERMANENT). A classical effect conditioned on a quantum predicate is non-physical — same family as the measure/return/break/goto escapes — so loud decline is the CORRECT end state, not a stopgap (no correct lowering exists). In armEscapesOrCollect, diagnose any in-arm instruction that is not a cq_phi gate, the well-formed fall-through terminator, or a provably side-effect-free pure value (DiagnosticInfoUnsupported 'classical side effect under quantum control', or fold into the existing escape diagnostic). Also escape-guard the nested-AND Mid block (currently only Arm is guarded).

LOWER-CONFIDENCE SIBLINGS (NOT reproduced from clang -O1; defensive-only — file separately only if desired, do NOT block this bug): (a) a tainted br/select whose condition is an and-i1 / or-i1 / xor-i1 or a non-CmpInst i1 (trunc) -> ControlFlag.cpp:91-93 returns false silently -> downstream OpcodeLowering rewrite -> broken module (could NOT reach from clang -O1: a `(fa & fb) ? a : b` source canonicalized to a clean select-i1 that lowered fine). (b) interprocedural/wrapped measurement: isMeasureCall (ControlDetection.cpp:60-69) matches direct callees named cq_measure_/cqrt_measure_ only, so an un-inlined wrapper that calls measure inside an arm is not recognized (low likelihood at -O1).

BUG (confirmed silent miscompile, clang -O1 reachable). A nested wide-int (i64) data mux — an outer tainted-condition select whose arms are the i32-laundered RESULTS of inner dissolveSelect reductions of i64 data — is lowered at i32 width: a silent truncating width-collapse miscompile.

ROOT CAUSE. dissolveSelect registers its result as tainted (MergeDissolution.cpp:380) but NEVER records taint.HandleWidth[Res] (the only writer is RotationLowering.cpp:134 for theta handles). So for the OUTER mux, taint.HandleWidth.lookup(A) and lookup(B) both miss, and the width falls back to abiWidthFromType(A->getType()) = i32 (the laundered handle type) at MergeDissolution.cpp:264-272. The outer mux is then built with cqrt_alloc_i32(0) + cq_template_add_i32_controlled on registers whose LOGICAL width is i64. This is the WP11 width-collapse (test_C_libtooling-u6v.5) reopened for the nested-mux-arm case, which has NO fixture — mux_handles_i64.ll only tests DIRECT cq_theta arms (whose HandleWidth IS recorded).

REPRO (clang -O1, llvm@19 19.1.7, libCQPass.so @ b062f2d; /tmp/cqcheck/nested_mux.c):

  long long f(int c1, int c2, int c3, long long a, long long b, long long cc, long long d) {
      long long qa=cq_theta(a,0.1), qb=cq_theta(b,0.2), qc=cq_theta(cc,0.3), qd=cq_theta(d,0.4);
      int p1=cq_theta(c1,0.5), p2=cq_theta(c2,0.6), p3=cq_theta(c3,0.7);
      long long r = (p1>0) ? ((p2>0)?qa:qb) : ((p3>0)?qc:qd);
      return cq_measure(r);
  }

Lowered output: inner muxes are CORRECT (cqrt_alloc_i64 + cq_template_add_i64_controlled), but the OUTER mux emits
  %h16 = call i32 @cqrt_alloc_i32(i32 0)
  cq_template_add_i32_controlled(..., %h_sel8 /*i64*/) ; and again for %h_sel13
then cqrt_measure_i64 reads it. The top 32 bits of the i64 result are computed with i32-width controlled-add templates. opt -passes=verify CLEAN, exit 0, NO diagnostic.

RELATED CRASH (same root cause): the MIXED (mux.1) nested form — outer select with one i64-laundered tainted arm and one classical i64 arm — instead aborts the module verifier (cq_template_sub_i32_hl(i32 handle, i64 99) + cqrt_alloc_i32(i64 99) type mismatch -> report_fatal_error "Broken module"). Same fix resolves it.

RECOMMENDED FIX (per-gap optimal, user-chosen 2026-06-03 = LOWER CORRECTLY; cheap, no capability lost). Add `taint.HandleWidth[Res] = AbiWidth;` immediately after MergeDissolution.cpp:381 so a downstream mux/compare recovers the logical width. Defense-in-depth (optional): make dissolveSelect's both-tainted/mixed width-miss a loud diagnoseNoTemplate instead of the silent abiWidthFromType-of-laundered-type fallback, matching ControlFlag.cpp:37-40's report_fatal_error treatment of the same HandleWidth staleness (risk R3).
